---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import EventFeed from '../../components/EventFeed.astro';
import NewsWire from '../../components/NewsWire.astro';
import data from '../../data/events.json';
---

<Base
	image="/og/events.png"
	title="News"
	description="Dated log of the events that moved crypto, each one paired with the measured market reaction rather than a headline."
	keywords={['crypto news', 'market reaction', 'bitcoin events', 'crypto event log', 'measured impact']}
>
	<div class="wrap page">
		<header class="ph">
			<p class="label">kept by hand since {data.since}</p>
			<h1>News</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Not a news feed. Every entry was read off a primary source, and where it claims a market
				reaction that number was measured against exchange data with the window named. If an
				event moved nothing, it says so.
			</p>
		</header>

		<div class="panel body">
			<EventFeed heading />
		</div>

		<div class="panel body">
			<NewsWire heading />
		</div>

		<section class="method">
			<h3>Why it is short</h3>
			<p>
				Aggregated crypto headlines are free and worthless — a hundred outlets rewriting the same
				wire in a race to publish. What is missing from all of them is the second half: what the
				tape actually did. That takes pulling the bars around the event, so it goes at the speed
				one person can verify things, and the log starts the day I started keeping it rather than
				being backfilled from memory.
			</p>
		</section>

	</div>
</Base>

<style>
	.page { padding-top: 48px; max-width: 840px; }
	.ph { max-width: 62ch; margin-bottom: 26px; }
	.ph h1 { margin: 10px 0 14px; }
	.lede { color: var(--fg-dim); margin: 0; }
	.body { padding: 22px 24px 24px; }
	.secmark { margin: 34px 0 12px; }
	.secmark:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }
	.secmark h2 {
		margin: 0 0 5px; font-size: 1.28rem;
	}
	.secmark p {
		margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--fg-mute); line-height: 1.6; max-width: 70ch;
	}
	.method {
		margin-top: 34px; padding: 20px 22px;
		border: 1px dashed var(--line-bright); border-radius: var(--radius);
	}
	.method h3 { margin: 0 0 10px; font-size: 1rem; }
	.method p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.87rem; color: var(--fg-dim); line-height: 1.7; }
</style>
